{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze feels like a natural follow-up to Old Sock because relaxed blues and the JJ Cale connection fit what I want to hear today.",
    "The Muddy Waters collaboration, Blue & Lonesome, and the Dire Straits and Mark Knopfler collection connect with my interest in blues guitar and roots songwriting."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Endless River's atmospheric instrumental direction misses my current preference for blues-oriented songs, even though rock is part of my listening history.",
    "Django and Jimmie stretches my interest in Blown Away into a desire for traditional country duets that I do not feel today.",
    "Powerful People, New, and Blues do not give me enough certainty about the music to choose them during a brief visit; that uncertainty does not necessarily mean I would dislike them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in established rock musicians seems to have been treated as interest in a broad range of their musical directions.",
    "My interaction with Blown Away seems to have been taken as a broader appetite for country releases than it supports."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection to Old Sock matters especially today: I want relaxed blues, guitar playing, and roots songwriting.",
    "I am choosing only one album and currently prefer a studio release over a live recording or a compilation, even when the artists appeal to me."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my blues and guitar interests, but spread too broadly beyond the relaxed studio album I want today."
}"}
